    <statement><p>The pie chart represents a school<rsq/>s student population.</p>
<!-- PTX:WARNING: PGML wanted to center align here. -->
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/section-fractions-and-fraction-arithmetic-9-6-15-image-1.png" width="83%"/>
<p><fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/> more of the school is white students than black students.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>{\frac{1}{8}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>By the pie chart, the school has <m>{{\frac{3}{8}}}</m> white students, and <m>{{\frac{1}{4}}}</m> black students.</p>
<p>We will use subtraction to find the difference:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\begin{aligned}[t]
   \amp \phantom{{}=}{{\frac{3}{8}}}-{{\frac{1}{4}}} \\
   \amp = \frac{3 \cdot 1}{8 \cdot 1} - \frac{1 \cdot 1}{4 \cdot 1} \\
   \amp = \frac{3}{8} - \frac{2}{8} \\
   \amp = \frac{3-2}{8} \\
   \amp = \frac{1}{8} \\ 
\end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
</solution>
